# qualification's re-score (core/modules/qualification/README.md "The re-score"): after a criteria
# save, the worker scores the scored leads again from their stored verdicts with the current
# criteria, with no model call and no credits. `pnpm rescore --workspace <slug> [--person <id>]`
# does the same. The route is @Idempotent(): the same Idempotency-Key answers the first answer again
# for a day. A write sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too.
# `personId` is a person of your workspace with a lead: put it in http-client.private.env.json.

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/qualification/rescore: every scored lead of the workspace
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/qualification/rescore
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000040

{}

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/qualification/rescore: the named persons only, up to 500
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/qualification/rescore
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041

{ "personIds": ["{{personId}}"] }
